## Craft audit: Persuade pages and redesigns

Run this in Phases 1-6, on every audited page, when a page is Persuade (the classifier in the Design Hard Rules) or the user asked for a redesign or a craft audit. It adds what generated sites ship and a reviewer catches in seconds: invented content, missing ship basics, scroll-listener reveals, `100vh`, and a Persuade page's conversion basics. Its rules render from /design-html's craft section, so a page is audited against the rules it was built to.

### 1. Run the craft check on each page

With a URL, save the page in the script that opens it. Aside: add `await fs.writeFile(path.join(pwd, "{page}.page.html"), await pg.content());`. Fallback engine: `_TMP=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/gstack-craft.XXXXXX"); $B js 'document.documentElement.outerHTML' --out "$_TMP/{page}.page.html" --raw`. With no running app, use the page's HTML file in the repo. Then:

```bash
{{BIN_DIR}}/gstack-design-craft <path-to-page.html>
```

Each `CRAFT_CHECK: <id> <count> <fix>` line is one category 9 finding under that id; `CRAFT_RESULT: clean` adds none. For a /design-html page with a `finalized.json` beside it, add `--accepted <finalized.json>`: each `CRAFT_ACCEPTED` line is a finding the user already accepted, listed with its reason, not filed again. Exit 2 (framework source, an empty or unreadable file): say the check was unavailable for that page and judge the tells below by eye. A hit the user's real content explains (a customer named Nexus, a supplied 50% figure) is noted, not filed. Saved pages stay out of the report directory; delete them after the check.

